# Enterprise Multi-Layer Network Architecture

## Project Objective (Personal Statement)

In this project, I designed and implemented a complete enterprise-grade network 
from the Access layer to the Internet edge. My objective was to simulate a real-world 
corporate infrastructure including redundancy, dynamic routing, firewall high 
availability, dual ISP connectivity, and SD-WAN.
The goal was not only to make devices communicate, but to deeply understand 
how EIGRP, OSPF, and BGP interact together, how route redistribution works, 
and how high availability ensures business continuity.

This lab represents a real Enterprise Edge architecture that could be deployed 
in a medium or large organization.

