## Routing Architecture Overview
LAN Routing:

I implemented EIGRP AS 100 between Distribution and Core switches
to provide fast convergence and internal scalability.

Core to Firewall:
I used OSPF Area 0 between Core and ASA. The Core redistributes 
EIGRP into OSPF and the ASA redistributes connected routes.

Internet Edge:
FortiGate runs BGP AS 65010 and peers with Transit routers (AS 65020).
Transit routers peer with:
  - ISP Verizon (AS 64512)
  - ISP AT (AS 64513)
This provides full dual-ISP redundancy.

## High Availability Design

ASA High Availability:
Configured in Active/Standby mode.
Failover interface: Gig0/1
Failover network: 13.13.13.0/29

FortiGate High Availability:
Active/Passive cluster.
Heartbeat interface: port3
Session pickup enabled.
Configuration fully synchronized.
This ensures firewall redundancy at both internal and perimeter layers.

## SD-WAN & NAT Implementation
SD-WAN is enabled on FortiGate with two WAN members:
  - port5 (Primary - WAN1)
  - port6 (Secondary - WAN2)
Priority mode ensures WAN1 is preferred unless SLA fails.

NAT Policy:
LAN traffic → virtual-wan-link
NAT enabled for secure Internet access.
